        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0327" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-17T10:00:00+08:00">May 17, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>675. Following from Hankow.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“May 16, noon. Reference telegram May 13, 7 a.m. from Foochow regarding
                        protection of Americans there. Please expedite reply, repeat Foochow’s
                        telegram to Tokyo and add following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>‘Unless you see reasons to the contrary, I suggest that it would he
                                advisable to notify Japanese Government of concentration of American
                                nationals at Tsangchienshan at Foochow, and in addition supply list
                                of places in the interior at which Americans now are.’</p>
                        </quote></p>
                    <p>You will doubtless wish to make similar communication to the Japanese
                        authorities at Shanghai. Please repeat to Washington. Johnson.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
